+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` checks the model's tool input against the registered definition's `inputSchema` before the executor runs. This spec states the contract the registry must honour, so that a malformed call is answered in one known way the model can read and correct.
+
+## Rejections
+
+- A call whose input is missing a property the schema requires is answered with a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names that property as required, and the executor is never invoked ([validated by: returns a rejection naming a missing required property and never invokes the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L54)).
+- A call whose property has the wrong type is rejected with a `result` naming the property path and the expected type, and the `result` never contains the offending value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property with its path and expected type, never echoing the value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L66)).
+- A rejection is a tool result, not an exception: `execute` resolves, and the rejection text reaches the provider on the next round of the tool loop, so a corrected retry completes the turn ([validated by: hands a rejected tool call to the model as a result, so a corrected retry completes the turn](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L116)).
+
+## Schema compilation
+
+- A static tool whose `inputSchema` cannot be compiled makes `register` throw, naming the tool, so a broken schema fails at startup rather than mid-conversation ([validated by: throws at register time for an uncompilable schema, naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L79)).
+- A tool whose definition is a function is validated on each call against the schema that function returns at that call, not against a schema cached from an earlier call ([validated by: validates each call against the schema its source returns at that call, not a cached one](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L91)).
